.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# lexical.sqlite grows past GitHub's 50 MB limit — regenerate with: python3 scripts/skill_sync.py --all
# Glob, not the literal path: it also covers SQLite's -wal/-shm sidecars and the
# empty stray a mistyped `sqlite3 vector_index/lexical.sqlite3 ...` leaves behind
# (the CLI creates the file as a side effect of being handed a missing name).
vector_index/lexical.sqlite*

# chunks.jsonl crosses GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold (~98 MB at 690 skills
# and growing). Regenerate locally or in CI via `python3 scripts/build_index.py`
# before any validation or drift check. registry/ + vector_index/manifest.json
# stay committed — they encode the content hash that detects rebuild drift,
# so CI can verify reproducibility without the raw bytes.
vector_index/chunks.jsonl

# Clone cost, measured 2026-07-31 — what these ignores fix and what they don't.
# `.git` is 524 MB (`du -sh .git`; `git count-objects -vH` → size-pack
# 389.86 MiB). Reachable history holds 13,709 MB of blob bytes and ONE path is
# 85.0% of it: vector_index/chunks.jsonl, 206 committed revisions totalling
# 11,651 MB uncompressed, last tracked at 59e265ce6. lexical.sqlite adds 962 MB
# across 30 revisions (last tracked at 27e89cda7). registry/skills.json is
# 766 MB across 221 revisions and stays tracked BY DESIGN — it encodes the
# content hash that detects rebuild drift — so it is now the largest *growing*
# tracked artifact; revisit it before adding anything else of that shape.
#
# The rules above stop future growth. They cannot shrink an existing clone:
# the bytes are already in the pack. Only a history rewrite (git filter-repo,
# git lfs migrate) would reclaim them, and that is deliberately out of scope —
# it rewrites every SHA and invalidates every existing clone, fork, and the
# commit refs cited in MASTER_QUEUE.md and elsewhere in the docs.
# Reproduce: git rev-list --objects --all | join against
#   git cat-file --batch-check --batch-all-objects, then sum per path.

# embeddings.jsonl holds 384-dim fastembed vectors for every chunk
# (~500 MB at 120K chunks). Same pattern as chunks.jsonl — regenerate via
# `python3 scripts/skill_sync.py --all`. The content_hash on each record
# enables incremental re-encode of only changed chunks on subsequent runs.
vector_index/embeddings.jsonl

# skill_embeddings.jsonl holds one 384-dim vector per skill (~3 MB at 994
# skills). Built ~100x faster than chunk-level embeddings.jsonl and useful
# as a lightweight semantic-rerank signal when chunk-level isn't available.
# Regenerate via `python3 scripts/build_skill_embeddings.py`.
vector_index/skill_embeddings.jsonl

# Export tree is a generated artifact (~130 MB for claude+mcp+cursor+windsurf+
# aider+augment at 684 skills). Consumers regenerate via:
#   python3 scripts/export_skills.py --all
# The committed registry/export_manifest.json records per-target content hashes
# so CI parity checks don't need the bytes — just the hashes.
exports/

# Claude Code worktrees (temporary agent working copies)
.claude/worktrees/

# Codex ↔ Claude Code handoff zone: raw skill file drops (=== FILE: ... ===
# format) that Claude Code picks up, writes into the tree, syncs, validates,
# and commits. Processed files go under _codex_drops/processed/. The zone
# itself is tracked (README + prompt) but individual drops are not.
_codex_drops/*.txt
_codex_drops/*.out
_codex_drops/processed/

# Per-run reports generated by scripts/run_builder.py — each gated run writes
# REQUIREMENTS.md, state.json, envelope.json, report.md under
# docs/reports/<agent>/<run_id>/. Transient CI/debug artifacts; regenerate via:
#   python3 scripts/run_builder.py --agent <agent> --fixture <...> --emitted-dir <...>
docs/reports/

# scripts/execute_agent_fixture.py debug artifact — the assembled prompt sent
# to the model. Reproducible from the fixture + agent source, ~37 KB per run,
# noisy to diff. The raw.md (model response), envelope.json (extracted
# envelope), and grade.txt (grader verdict) alongside it ARE committed as the
# persistent record of each agent execution.
docs/validation/agent_executions_*/*.prompt.txt

# .claude/ is local Claude Code session state by default (user-specific, not
# part of the repo). Three subtrees are exceptions and ARE committed:
#   .claude/agents/    generated by scripts/build_plugin.py — the run-time agent
#                      loaders. No tracked duplicate exists elsewhere.
#   .claude/skills/    generated by scripts/build_plugin.py — the 12 tiered
#                      router skills. No tracked duplicate exists elsewhere.
#   .claude/workflows/ the repo's named Workflow scripts (e.g. source-onboarding.js).
# The negations matter for more than the initial add: without them a NEW file
# written by build_plugin.py is invisible to `git status` and gets silently
# dropped from the next commit.
#
# Two of those three are PROJECT-LOCAL paths, not plugin paths. Be precise
# about which mechanism each one rides, because conflating them is what
# produced an earlier false "the plugin is verified working" claim. Measured
# 2026-08-01 on Claude Code 2.1.209 by installing this repo into an isolated
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and reading `claude plugin details sfskills`:
#   .claude/skills/    reaches the plugin ONLY because .claude-plugin/
#                      marketplace.json names it in the entry's `skills` field
#                      (the marketplace-root exception). Drop that field and
#                      the routers stop shipping.
#   .claude/agents/    does NOT reach the plugin at all, and never can. A
#                      plugin's subagents load from flat `agents/*.md` at the
#                      plugin ROOT and from nowhere else; every manifest key
#                      that claims to relocate them loads zero. These 48 files
#                      load for anyone whose cwd is this repo, plugin or not —
#                      exactly the mechanism that faked the earlier check.
#
# Which is why, as of 2026-08-07, build_plugin.py writes each loader TWICE:
# `.claude/agents/<id>.md` (project scope, the copy ignored by default here
# and rescued by the negation below) and `agents/<id>.md` at the repo root
# (plugin scope, never ignored). Same render call, byte-identical output. Both
# are needed and neither substitutes for the other: re-measured 2026-08-07 on
# 2.1.209 from outside the repo, `claude plugin details sfskills` went from
# `Agents (0)` to `Agents (48)` once the root-level copies existed.
# `python3 scripts/build_plugin.py --audit-install` is the standing gate — it
# fails if the two sets ever diverge, which matters because a project-local
# definition OVERRIDES a same-named plugin agent
# (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins), so drift is invisible from inside
# a clone.
#
# .claude/commands/ is deliberately NOT committed, and does NOT need to be for
# the plugin to ship slash commands. It is a byte-for-byte copy of the tracked
# `commands/*.md` (verified: 66/66 files identical, `cmp` clean), so tracking
# it would create a permanent drift surface between two copies of the same
# file. The plugin loads the commands from the tracked `commands/` instead —
# .claude-plugin/plugin.json declares `"commands": ["./commands/"]`, and a
# clean install measured `Skills (78)` = 12 routers + all 66 commands.
# .claude/commands/ is a local editor convenience, regenerated by
# `python3 scripts/bootstrap.py` (which calls scripts/install_local_commands.py).
#
# A blanket `dir/` ignore can't be negated for children, hence `/*` + `!`.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/workflows/

# Session artifacts from eval / build / audit runs.
# The harness scripts under evals/measurement/*.py STAY committed (reusable
# tooling). Their per-session OUTPUTS do not — they are dated, noisy in diff,
# and easily regenerated by re-running the script. If you want to reference
# a past session's output, archive it under /tmp or a personal scratch dir.
#
# Pattern reasoning: anything that ends in a dated report or per-loop dump
# belongs in this list. New report types should be added here, not committed.
evals/measurement/REPORT.md
evals/measurement/SESSION_REPORT.md
evals/measurement/REMEDIATION_PLAN.md
evals/measurement/EXISTING_SKILL_QUALITY_AUDIT.md
evals/measurement/gap_themes.md
evals/measurement/gap_screening_report.md
evals/measurement/competitive_*.md
evals/measurement/loop[0-9]*_*.json
evals/measurement/loop[0-9]*_*.md
evals/measurement/per_row.jsonl

# Multi-agent scaffold churn — when /build-skills or similar batch commands
# run, sub-agents may shuffle scaffolds between skills/ and .planning/ during
# authoring. Final skills go under skills/; partial work-in-progress is local
# until it's ready to ship via a normal /new-skill commit.
.planning/scaffolds-pending/

# Per-session metrics for the agentic build commands. Local-only history of
# which skills got built, agent failure rates, build durations. Used by
# /build-skills to track its own performance over time and improve, but never
# part of the production product.
.planning/build-history/

# Pre-prod / content QA session artifacts. The harness scripts under
# .planning/qa-execution/*.py are reusable but per-session in nature; their
# raw JSON results + venv + dated plan/report markdown are NOT product
# artifacts. Keep them local — they're easy to regenerate by re-running the
# harness against the target org.
.planning/qa-execution/
.planning/qa-*.md
.qa-venv/

# Per-machine venvs spun up by the v0.4.4 publish gate (L0-2 / L0-3) and
# similar release smoke-tests. Regenerated on every wheel build; never
# belong in the repo.
.build-venv/
.smoke-venv/
.verify-venv/

# `python -m build` output. Wheels + sdists are uploaded to PyPI from
# `mcp/sfskills-mcp/dist/` and don't need to live in git.
mcp/sfskills-mcp/dist/

# Pip's editable-install metadata bundle (`pip install -e .` writes this).
# Per-machine, regenerated on every install — never belongs in the repo.
*.egg-info/

# Session-local intake reports from scripts/onboard_source.py — never committed.
.intake-reports/
